      "evidence": "In template/scripts/execute_requirement.py, `_archive_delivered_task_state` has one call site, just before `start_managed_task.start_managed_task`. The sequential all-delivered path (`if not ordered:` after `_sequential_round`) returns `_await_post_merge`, `_retrospective_pending` or `reconcile_parent` without archiving. The last child's state therefore stays in the checkout while the Requirement waits for the retrospective, and it is only moved by a later child start. This matches the T1 spec wording (\"before advance starts a child\"), but it is narrower than the stated outcome.",
